values ('c3e4f5a6-7b8c-4d73-8e23-3f4a5b6c7d83', 'cognitive-psychology', 'Cognitive Psychology', 'Cognitive Psychology investigates how people perceive, attend, remember, represent knowledge, understand language, solve problems, reason, and choose. The course integrates classic experiments with contemporary cognitive neuroscience, computational modeling, open science, and real-world applications. A common conceptual spine serves both pathways: undergraduates build experimental literacy and transferable understanding; MA students add primary-literature synthesis, formal analysis, methodological critique, and independent research design.');

